# Hand-tuned theme token CSS: prettier's singleQuote:true rewrites this repo's
# double-quoted `data-theme="x"` attribute selectors to single quotes, which used
# to silently break themeTokens.ts's parser regex (now quote-agnostic as a second
# line of defense — see that file). Kept out of prettier's reach so these
# carefully-wrapped comments/alignment don't churn on an unrelated format pass.
packages/theme/src/themes.css
packages/theme/src/themes/*.css

# Everything below is written by a generator, not by hand. `pnpm format:check` is a gate on
# what we push, so anything a build or a script rewrites has to stay out of it — otherwise the
# next `tauri build` / `pnpm generate` / e2e run silently turns the tree unformatted again and
# the gate fails on a file nobody edited.

# Rewritten by every `tauri build`/`tauri dev` from the plugin ACLs (tracked, but not ours).
apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen/schemas

# packages/mascot/scripts/generate.mjs writes these from assets/parts/*.png; it doesn't pipe
# its output through prettier, so formatting them here would churn on the next `generate`.
packages/mascot/src/generated

# apps/docs/scripts/generate.ts renders these from apps/e2e/features/*.feature on every docs
# dev/build run. Gitignored as well — the .feature files are the committed source.
apps/docs/docs/features
apps/docs/.vitepress/sidebar.json
apps/docs/.vitepress/landing-css.json

# Rewritten by wdio's `onComplete` at the end of every e2e run, and committed as a reference
# snapshot (see the file's own header).
apps/e2e/REPORT.md

# The release scripts splice GitHub's release-notes API output into this file verbatim, and
# that API writes `* ` bullets where prettier wants `- `. Formatting it would mean every
# `pnpm release` pushes an unformatted CHANGELOG through its own pre-push gate.
CHANGELOG.md
